15. Where computation happens

One of the biggest advantages of this architecture is that there is no model inference.

You can implement almost everything using JavaScript:

TF-IDF → JavaScript
Cosine similarity → JavaScript
Graph construction → JavaScript
TextRank → JavaScript
Keyword scoring → JavaScript
Redundancy removal → JavaScript
Categorization → JavaScript

So:

No Hugging Face model
No model download
No GPU
No API key
No server
No inference cost

This makes it much more suitable for your browser extension.

16. One weakness you should know

Pure extractive summarization cannot genuinely understand semantics.

For example:

"We should use a transformer."

"I don't want to use a transformer."

Keyword-based systems see:

transformer
transformer

and may consider them highly related.

But their meanings are opposite.

Therefore, later we can improve your system with lightweight semantic techniques without immediately introducing an LLM.

Possible evolution:

V1
TF-IDF + TextRank

 ↓

V2
TF-IDF + TextRank + better heuristics

 ↓

V3
Sentence embeddings + TextRank

 ↓

V4
Hybrid extractive + small model

But don't jump to V3 yet.

First make V1 work extremely well.

17. What you should build first

Don't implement all of this simultaneously.

Build it in this order:

1. Transcript parser
 ↓
2. Sentence segmentation
 ↓
3. TF-IDF
 ↓
4. Cosine similarity
 ↓
5. TextRank
 ↓
6. Top sentence selection
 ↓
7. Redundancy removal
 ↓
8. Conversation-specific scoring
 ↓
9. Category assignment
 ↓
10. Final context formatting

Then test each stage independently.

Your first milestone should simply be:

Given a pasted conversation, select the 20–30 most important sentences without losing major decisions or requirements.

Once that works, the structured context layer becomes much easier.

The most important principle to keep in your notes is:

Selection happens first. Organization happens second. Compression happens last.

That keeps the system lightweight and makes it much easier to debug when the summary loses something important.

